  "status_text": "The 2n-cycle is now held between two checked bounds at every odd size n of at least 5: at least 2n - 1 + ceil((n - 1)/4) AND/OR gates of fan-in at most two, and at most (5n + 1)/2, roughly 9n/4 against 5n/2. Also checked in the last quarter hour: when one input of a circuit is fixed, every gate that turns constant, or reads a wire that did, is saved, unless what is left is true everywhere. What that step leaves open is narrow and named, a gate killed by the fixed input whose other input is still read elsewhere, and a search over the 5-cycle is testing it (computed).",
